we have drastically different populations
as well. It's so, so in the United States

00:08:28.270 --> 00:08:38.289
it's 4.43 deaths per hundred thousand people.
In the UK, I think it's 0.6 deaths per 100,000

00:08:38.289 --> 00:08:45.670
people. So it's absolutely population adjusted.
And so why do we have like 400 times more,

00:08:45.670 --> 00:08:51.899
uh, like deaths related to guns? If the UK
and the u s were playing the same amount of

00:08:51.899 --> 00:08:56.519
video games, it has to be something else.
And there are studies that show that, for

