00:12:23.410 --> 00:12:27.339
you know, people who spend a lot of time sort
of living on the internet also play video

00:12:27.339 --> 00:12:31.800
games because that's a major form of their
recreation. It's a major form of their community.

00:12:31.800 --> 00:12:36.160
And Video Games can build community both like
positive community and negative community.

00:12:36.160 --> 00:12:40.350
Um, I've worked with people who, you know,
have, have felt like the community they gained

00:12:40.350 --> 00:12:44.839
through the Internet is really important to
them. Um, so I think it's absolutely possible

00:12:44.839 --> 00:12:49.410
that it's kind of a third variable unrelated
to each of those, but as not causal. You,

00:12:49.410 --> 00:12:50.410
you talk

00:12:50.410 --> 00:12:54.680
about, um, uh, undiagnosed mental health stuff.
So without diagnosing any particular people

00:12:54.680 --> 00:12:58.420
or particular shooters, I, let's dig in a
little bit to the mental health thing because

00:12:58.420 --> 00:13:02.199
that's also a common talking point, which
is the problem of gun violence is mental health

00:13:02.199 --> 00:13:06.370
and not access to guns. One thing is, which
we don't have to get into that. A lot of the

00:13:06.370 --> 00:13:10.269
same people claiming that aren't doing anything
