00:13:58.279 --> 00:14:02.899
Right? Well, that I'm saying even if we could
establish that, then what do we do? So I'm

00:14:02.899 --> 00:14:07.069
not necessarily accepting it. I'm saying what
if, what if it were true? Then how would we

00:14:07.069 --> 00:14:08.379
even deal with that?

00:14:08.379 --> 00:14:13.160
Yeah. So I think that that becomes problematic
because when we talk about mental illness,

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:18.750
there are two kinds of mental illness. Like
you can lump mental illness into two big categories.

00:14:18.750 --> 00:14:23.060
One is personality disorders. So these are
not things that happen to you. These are part

00:14:23.060 --> 00:14:28.589
of who you are. So when we think of someone
like a sociopath or a psychopath, that's not

00:14:28.589 --> 00:14:32.800
a condition that someone sort of randomly
gets afflicted with. You can be like, for

00:14:32.800 --> 00:14:37.249
example, a postpartum mother and experienced
depression for the first time in your life,

00:14:37.249 --> 00:14:41.139
right? So some mental health issues or things
that sort of happen to you, you can develop

00:14:41.139 --> 00:14:46.019
anxiety, you can develop depression. And some
parts of what we consider mental health or

00:14:46.019 --> 00:14:50.709
mental illnesses are actually like baked into
